#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Writes this case's fixture data into the run's workspace (both arms see the same files).
# Generated by benchmarks/builder; edit the case script there, not this file.
set -euo pipefail
mkdir -p resources
cat > resources/notes.md <<'DEVILS_ANALYST_EOF'
# Notes
- Burrow & Bark Pet Supply, online pet food and accessories. Gross margin about 40% of revenue.
- Q3 = 29 June to 27 September 2026. Spend from the ad platforms; sessions and revenue from GA4 (last click).
- Microsoft Ads campaigns started on 10 August.
DEVILS_ANALYST_EOF
cat > resources/agency_budget_memo_q4.md <<'DEVILS_ANALYST_EOF'
# Q4 budget recommendation (agency memo)

Q3 return on ad spend, all figures from our reporting:

| Channel | Q3 spend | Revenue | ROAS | Source |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Google Ads | $89,767 | $590,850 | 6.6 | Google Ads conversion value |
| Meta | $61,015 | $54,806 | 0.90 | GA4, session source facebook / paid_social |
| Microsoft Ads | $8,652 | $0 | 0.0 | GA4, bing / cpc |

Every channel above a ROAS of 1.0 pays for itself.

Recommendation for Q4:
1. Cut Meta prospecting and retargeting entirely; move the $61,015 to Google Ads, which returns 6.6.
2. Stop Microsoft Ads (no revenue in GA4).
3. Organic Social (facebook.com referrals) has grown strongly since late July: add a part-time community manager.
DEVILS_ANALYST_EOF
